### 3.4 Worked certificate example

```
$ go run ./cmd/demo
weight       = 17
parent       = [-1 0 1 1]          # 0->1, 1->2, 1->3
tree edges   = [-1 0 2 4]
pi           = [0 10 14 9]         # π_r=0, π_a=10, π_b=14, π_c=9
vertex->set  = [-1 0 0 1]          # {a,b} in set 0; c in set 1; r in none
set parent   = [1 -1]              # set 0 ⊂ set 1
set z        = [2 7]               # z ≥ 0
verify       = <nil>
```

Interpretation (`r=0,a=1,b=2,c=3`; edges `r→a=10, a→b=5, b→a=1, a→c=2, c→a=3, r→b=100, r→c=100`):

- Dual objective `= π_a+π_b+π_c − (|S₀|−1)z₀ − (|S₁|−1)z₁ = 33 − 1·2 − 2·7 = 17 = w(T)`.
- Tree edges are tight, e.g. `b→a`: `w=1`, `π_a − (z₀+z₁) = 10−9 = 1`. ✅
- Non-tree `c→a`: `w=3`, `π_a − (z₀+z₁) = 1 ≤ 3`. ✅
- Since the reduced cost is non-negative on every edge and the dual objective equals `w(T)`, LP duality proves `T` is a minimum arborescence.

